WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:11.559
Hey there everyone!

00:00:11.559 --> 00:00:22.430
In this episode I am going to talk about my
personal Top 20 lessons that I learned from

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:27.720
the book "Emotional Intelligence" Why It Can
Matter More Than IQ, by Daniel Goleman.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.660
Does IQ define our destiny?

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:35.820
In his groundbreaking bestseller, Daniel Goleman
argues that our view of human intelligence

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.120
is far too narrow.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:43.870
It is not our IQ, but our emotional intelligence
that plays a major role in thought, decision-making

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:46.579
and individual success.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:53.031
Self-awareness, impulse control, persistence,
motivation, empathy and social deftness: all

00:00:53.031 --> 00:00:58.710
are qualities that mark people who excel,
whose relationships flourish, who can navigate

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:03.410
difficult conversations, who become stars
in the workplace.

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:09.360
With new insights into the brain architecture
underlying emotion and rationality, Goleman

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:14.250
shows precisely how emotional intelligence
can be nurtured and strengthened in all of

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:15.890
us.

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:18.409
Lesson number 1 - Rational and Emotional

00:01:18.409 --> 00:01:22.439
It is mentioned in the book that there are
two different bits of intelligence.

00:01:22.439 --> 00:01:28.250
Throughout our lives, we make decisions by
being influenced by these two types of intelligence.

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:32.430
Who we are, what we do, our reactions depend
entirely on it.

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:33.430
The underlying reason for our very clever
actions or our irrational but feel-good behaviors

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:34.430
depends on these two types of intelligence.

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:35.610
Lesson number 2 IQ Isn’t As Important As
We Think

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:38.780
IQ can’t get you beyond being a good employee.

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:43.000
It makes you graduate from school, but it
can’t find you a job.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:48.620
When you go to the job interview, your diploma
cannot answer the questions during the interview.

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:49.620
You need to have good communication with the
person who will hire you.

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:50.620
It all depends on your emotional intelligence.

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:53.920
Lesson number 3 Areas of Emotional Intelligence

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:59.740
Emotional intelligence is responsible for
our motivation, awareness, empathy, and relationships.

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:03.970
They’re all interconnected, and if you’re
bad at one, you’re more likely to be bad

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:04.979
at the others.

00:02:04.979 --> 00:02:08.679
Lesson number 4 The Emotional Brain Is Stronger

00:02:08.679 --> 00:02:13.670
The outer upper part of our brain is the part
where we make rational decisions, while the

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:17.550
lower part is the part where we make emotional
decisions.

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:22.790
No matter how rational beings we may appear,
we can very easily be deceived by the emotional

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:23.790
brain.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:24.790
We can find excuses to trick the rational
brain into doing what the emotional brain

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:25.790
wants.

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:26.790
Lesson number 5 Others’ Feelings

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:29.290
Thanks to our empathy, we can truly understand
how others are feeling.

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:33.990
If we could not distinguish between happy
or angry people, there would be incredible

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:35.440
chaos.

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:38.650
Beyond these two basic emotions, we must develop
an ability to empathize.

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:39.730
In the absence of empathy, our communication
aspect is affected very badly.

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:41.031
Lesson number 6 Motivation

00:02:41.031 --> 00:02:46.960
Our motivation, which enables us to endure
the problems we face for a long time, is also

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:49.230
a product of emotional intelligence.

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:52.790
We can convince ourselves that we can solve
problems.

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:56.180
We can remain optimistic and have hope for
the future.

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:58.060
Lesson number 7 Awareness

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:02.190
One of our most difficult aspects to develop
is our awareness.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:05.489
We must practice understanding how we truly
feel.

00:03:05.489 --> 00:03:08.140
We must ask ourselves questions.

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:09.430
We must listen to ourselves.

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:10.541
Lesson number 8 Relationships

00:03:10.541 --> 00:03:12.069
Relationships cannot be let go.

00:03:12.069 --> 00:03:13.700
It must be managed.

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:16.819
This requires mutual tolerance and understanding.

00:03:16.819 --> 00:03:22.510
If you know how to resolve conflicts, it turns
into a happy relationship for both parties.

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:24.299
Lesson number 9 Negative and Positive Emotions

00:03:24.299 --> 00:03:29.660
Our emotions change every moment, but the
longer negative emotions stay, the more negatively

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:31.590
they affect our lives.

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:35.980
It prevents us from being successful in our
work and relationships.

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:38.769
Fortunately, these feelings are not difficult
to change.

00:03:38.769 --> 00:03:42.969
You can learn to turn negative emotions into
positive ones.

00:03:42.969 --> 00:03:45.090
Lesson number 10 Productivity

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:50.690
When your emotional intelligence gets stronger,
your creativity starts to increase.

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:56.459
Regardless of your field of work, you will
start to see serious differences in your productivity.

00:03:56.459 --> 00:03:58.480
It will increase your performance.

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:00.610
Longer hours allow you to work with the same
efficiency.

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:01.610
Lesson number 11 Emotional Intelligence Is
The Key To Success

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:06.790
Since we cannot live a life independent of
our emotions, the higher our emotional intelligence,

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:09.489
the higher our quality of life will be.

00:04:09.489 --> 00:04:13.360
We know that successful managers are experts
in managing their emotional intelligence.

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:14.360
You can also take them as an example.

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:15.360
Lesson number 12 Leadership

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:18.790
A commander cannot direct an entire army by
saying “we are going to war”.

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:22.200
You can’t manage a team by just saying what
to do.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:26.710
You need to understand your team’s current
feelings and level of motivation.

00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:28.540
You should encourage them to work.

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:31.330
You have to use your emotional intelligence
for all of these.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:32.330
Lesson number 13 Teams

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:36.850
Average talent teams that get along well with
each other are more productive than gifted

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:38.900
teams that don’t get along.

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:43.400
It doesn’t matter how well a team with low
emotional intelligence is in control of the

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:44.570
numbers.

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:46.670
They can’t even decide what to try to do.

00:04:46.670 --> 00:04:47.670
Lesson number 14 Stress

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:51.710
Difficulties at work and in our relationships
put us under stress.

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:55.600
Stress makes it difficult for us to find solutions
to problems.

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:59.270
When we can’t find solutions to problems,
we get more stressed.

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:03.820
To get rid of this dead end, we need to know
how to manage our stressful situations.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:05.280
Lesson number 15 Marriage

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:10.570
The secret of long and happy marriages is
sincerity in your feelings.

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:15.350
If your marriage was not built on this basis
of honesty from the very beginning, it will

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:17.170
begin to crack over the years.

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:20.190
Even small problems become unsolvable.

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:23.150
You have to be emotionally open at the beginning
of the road.

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:24.640
Lesson number 16 Leadership

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:26.820
Leadership does not mean dominance.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:31.260
Leading your colleagues to a common goal and
making them believe in the reality of this

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:32.800
purpose.

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:37.550
Successful leaders are those who can keep
their team’s motivation alive for many years.

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:39.970
You have to make them desire the work to be
done.

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:42.430
Lesson number 17 Emotions Are All Normal

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:45.180
Anger, hatred, love, happiness…

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:52.010
You can understand when and under what circumstances
these feelings will emerge by following yourself.

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:57.270
You may have these feelings depending on how
you interpret the events you encounter.

00:05:57.270 --> 00:06:02.050
The important thing is to be able to react
independently of your feelings.

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:06.830
You may find yourself making promises that
you cannot keep because you are happy, or

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:08.713
you may resort to violence when you are angry.

00:06:08.713 --> 00:06:11.580
Lesson number 18 Being able to Express Your
Emotions

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:14.710
Not everyone’s level of empathy can be very
good.

00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:17.520
You may be in a difficult situation immediately.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:21.099
You may feel bad, but people may not understand
it.

00:06:21.099 --> 00:06:25.150
In these situations, you may need to express
your feelings a little more directly.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:26.789
Lesson number 19 You Are Not Your Emotions

00:06:26.789 --> 00:06:30.699
Keep doing what you need to do, no matter
how you feel.

00:06:30.699 --> 00:06:35.449
Success is achieved by people who cannot give
up no matter what their feelings and thoughts

00:06:35.449 --> 00:06:36.449
are.

00:06:36.449 --> 00:06:38.210
Don’t let your feelings affect your actions.

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:39.449
Lesson number 20 Timing

00:06:39.449 --> 00:06:44.080
As soon as you feel a different emotion, try
to think before you act.

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:49.139
Because emotional intelligence moves faster
than rational intelligence, it can make you

00:06:49.139 --> 00:06:53.610
act irrationally and make you say any unnecessary
words.

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:58.699
In this podcast, we discussed the key takeaways
from the book "Emotional Intelligence" by

00:06:58.699 --> 00:07:00.150
David Goleman.

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:06.870
We explored the definition of emotional intelligence
and its importance in personal and professional

00:07:06.870 --> 00:07:07.889
success.

00:07:07.889 --> 00:07:13.979
We also discussed the five components of emotional
intelligence, including self-awareness, self-regulation,

00:07:13.979 --> 00:07:18.210
motivation, empathy, and social skills.

00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:23.490
Through examples and case studies, we learned
how emotional intelligence can be developed

00:07:23.490 --> 00:07:26.460
and improved over time.

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:33.120
Overall, emotional intelligence is a crucial
skill for individuals to develop and can have

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:38.449
a significant impact on their personal and
professional lives.

00:07:38.449 --> 00:07:42.150
Thank you all for tuning in!

00:07:42.150 --> 00:07:55.530
Until next time, take care!

